abstract: >-
  QGIS plugin to map seagrass meadows and shallow benthic habitats from satellite
  imagery: download and preparation of Sentinel-2 surface reflectance, Landsat 4-9
  Collection 2 Level-2 import, ACOLITE import or any multiband reflectance raster,
  sunglint correction, median composites with a water-clarity ranking of the scenes,
  Lyzenga depth-invariant index, optional bottom texture, supervised classification
  with a three-state depth mask (bottom visible, not visible, too deep), spatial-block
  validation, stratified random validation points, error-corrected areas (Olofsson et
  al., 2014), change between two class maps and export of the maps to polygons.
keywords:
  - seagrass
  - benthic habitat mapping
  - Sentinel-2
  - QGIS
  - water column correction
  - accuracy assessment
